487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348160 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\nII. $AE=EA={I}_{3}$\n\nIII. $B={A}^{-1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348160 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3b65f93-463c-54d1-85ca-57a9749888f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348160 #edb/ref 1074 "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AE=EA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AE & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ -10 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
